# SEO & Page Standard

## Single source of truth

- Brand, URL, and contact data live in `src/config/site.ts`. Never hardcode the domain;
  use `SITE_URL` / `absoluteUrl()`. The domain comes from `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL`.
- Shared JSON-LD builders live in `src/lib/schema.ts` and render through
  `@@/components/common/JsonLd` (server-rendered, so crawlers see it in the HTML).

## Page architecture (same as AVR)

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `src/app/<route>/page.tsx` | Server component, no top-level `"use client"` |
| `src/app/<route>/layout.tsx` | Optional: route `metadata` + JSON-LD when shared by nested pages |
| `src/data/<name>.ts` | Copy, cards, FAQ arrays, plus `*_PAGE_URL` and `*_SEO` constants |
| `src/components/<feature>/*` | Small sections; `"use client"` only for real interactivity |

## Pre-launch: only the coming-soon page is indexed

- `/` (countdown coming-soon page) is the only indexable page and the only sitemap entry.
- **Every page built before launch goes in `src/app/dev/<page>/` and is served at
  `/dev/<page>`** (the future homepage is `/dev/home`). The `dev/layout.tsx` sets
  `noindex, nofollow`, and `next.config.ts` adds `X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow` for `/dev/**`,
  so new dev pages are covered automatically.
- Add the page to `DevRoutes` in `src/config/routes.ts` and to the list in `src/app/dev/page.tsx`.
- Do not override `robots` in dev page metadata, and do not add dev pages to `sitemap.ts`.
- `/dev` is disallowed in `robots.txt` (`src/app/robots.ts`) and also served with noindex;
  keep both.
- Do not link to `/dev` pages from the public coming-soon page.
- The launch date lives only in `SITE.launchDate` (`src/config/site.ts`, overridable via
  `NEXT_PUBLIC_LAUNCH_DATE`); never hardcode it elsewhere.

### Launching a page

1. Move it from `src/app/dev/<page>` to its final path (e.g. `dev/home` becomes `src/app/page.tsx`,
   `dev/about` becomes `src/app/about`), and update internal links.
2. Remove it from `DevRoutes` and the `/dev` index list.
3. Add it to `ROUTES` in `src/app/sitemap.ts`.
4. Complete the checklist below (metadata, canonical, OG, JSON-LD).

## Every new public page must

1. Export `metadata` (or `generateMetadata`) with a unique `title` (50-60 chars; the root
   template adds `| Med Gold`), a unique `description` (140-160 chars), and
   `alternates.canonical` set to the absolute page URL.
2. Override `openGraph` / `twitter` title, description, and URL when they differ from
   the defaults; add a route-level `opengraph-image.tsx` when the page deserves its own card.
3. Be added to `ROUTES` in `src/app/sitemap.ts`.
4. Include JSON-LD where relevant: `webPageSchema()` at minimum; `MedicalClinic`,
   `Physician`, `MedicalProcedure`, `FAQPage`, or `BreadcrumbList` when the content matches.
   FAQPage only when the page visibly shows the FAQ.
5. Have exactly one `h1`, a logical `h2`/`h3` order, and descriptive link text.
6. Use `next/image` with explicit `width`/`height` (or `fill` + `sizes`), meaningful `alt`,
   and `priority` only for the above-the-fold hero image.
7. Stay statically rendered unless data truly requires otherwise. Verify with `npm run build`
   and check the page source for the content and JSON-LD.

## Do not

- Do not add static `public/robots.txt` or `public/sitemap.xml`; they are generated by
  `src/app/robots.ts` and `src/app/sitemap.ts`.
- Do not load fonts from a Google Fonts `<link>`; use `next/font`.
- Do not add analytics scripts directly. GTM loads from `NEXT_PUBLIC_GTM_ID`. Microsoft Clarity loads
 through `@microsoft/clarity` in `ClarityInit`, using `CLARITY_PROJECT_ID` from `src/config/site.ts`
 (overridable via `NEXT_PUBLIC_CLARITY_ID`), on the production site only.
- Non-indexable pages (thank-you, 404, previews) must set `robots: { index: false }`
  and stay out of the sitemap.
